WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.330
Coral reefs cover only about 1
per cent of the world's oceans.

2
00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:08.770
Yet they are home to at least
25 per cent of marine life.

3
00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:13.650
They are built by animals: polyps
that lay down limestone skeletons.

4
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.230
Off north-east Australia, one great reef
system is made up of about 3,000 individual

5
00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:20.390
reefs.

6
00:00:20.440 --> 00:00:23.490
So what decides where
coral reefs can grow?

7
00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:26.250
In this mission, you'll
map where reefs are found,

8
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.650
and test the conditions they need.

9
00:00:28.700 --> 00:00:33.490
Then you'll follow that reef system
through four natural threats to its health.

10
00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.800
Your mission: find out what
decides where coral reefs can grow.
